+## Forgejo
+
+This queries the release API of a Forgejo or Gitea instance (for example
+codeberg.org or code.forgejo.org).  The Identifier matches the
+organisation/repositoryname on the Instance.  The default behaviour is to use
+the release the instance marks as latest.  This can be changed below with
+`use-tag: true`.
+
+```yaml
+package:
+  name: forgejo
+  version: 16.0.5
+  epoch: 0
+
+...
+
+update:
+  enabled: true
+  forgejo: # alternative today are `github:`, `git:` and `release_monitor:`
+    instance: https://codeberg.org # Mandatory, base URL of the Forgejo or Gitea instance
+    identifier: forgejo/forgejo # Mandatory, org/repo on the instance
+    strip-prefix: v # Optional, if the version obtained from the update service contains a prefix which should be ignored
+    strip-suffix: ignore_me # Optional, if the version obtained from the update service contains a suffix which should be ignored
+    use-tag: true # Optional, override the default of using the latest release to identify the version.  Not all projects use releases but just use tags
+    tag-filter-prefix: v17.2 # Optional, filter to apply when searching tags with a prefix on the instance, some repos maintain a mixture of tags for different major versions for example
+    tag-filter-contains: foo # Optional, filter to apply when searching tags with any match on the instance, some repos maintain a mixture of tags for different major versions for example
+```
+
 ## Git
 
 Git uses vanilla git to check for updates.  This is useful for projects that use unsupported Git Provider APIs.
